Z||000000||GT GT 87||03-17-2001||07:55 PM||||Well I finally joined a Fiero Club , they really are great people. (NIFE) Well driving there I was late and ran about 75-77 mph. After about 20 min. the check engine lite came on. Going home I kept it at 69-70 mph.No lite. When I got home -checked codes and found 13 & 32. Ox. sensor and EGR.  Any ideas? Idles great ,but never got the mileage of my other GT's. Any ideas would be great  thanks       STEVE||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||03-17-2001||08:24 PM||||Welcome to the 32 error code of the Fiero. I have an intermiitant highway induced 32 code problem no 13 code O2 sensor was replaced.  I've been replacing vacuum lines and most recently the EGR solinoid.  My EGR tube was replace in 96 I think, EGR valve in 98.  A vacuum leak may be causing the 13 code and may be asking for more gas  ECM reading lean mix. Hence bad gas milage.  For me I get great gas milage over the road with my GT (30-33 mpg).  Since my errors are intermittant (as yours seem to be) tracking down the cause is a pain.  With the new EGR solinoid, I'll see this week it code 32 is back.||||reg||6
